2026-10-26 09:03:54.0770 - DEBUG - graphrag.api.index - [{'id': 'b0ca2833340d32052483734b1b8da42c68a1c07301275a958e578d6f2c0fd975e493c187c9ff97eccc86068941a056a4823f2ae5c2bf0d4f3c3377d8d1840cc6', 'human_readable_id': 0, 'text': 'Distributed Systems: Service Reliability\n\n    A distributed system consists of services communicating over a network.\n    Service A calls Service B through an API gateway. The API gateway\n    routes requests and can enforce timeouts and rate limits.\n\n    Retries can improve reliability when transient failures occur.\n    However, uncontrolled retries can increase load and amplify outages.\n    Exponential backoff and jitter reduce synchronized retry attempts.\n\n    Circuit breakers prevent repeated calls to a failing dependency.\n    When the failure rate crosses a configured threshold', 'n_tokens': 100, 'document_id': 'b9c6f611addc84d60357c829e042254e47efbb01ea0825b99b0042d291db2339ea14650a903d05fc44a9f7e5bfc01460885d02298dbb5e34ecb6abbafe35d745', 'entity_ids': ['c1422f9b-4dee-45de-914b-af982169e32f', 'b4b8a309-85d2-44f6-9b66-5db3a9aa5e75'], 'relationship_ids': ['1139e482-b5aa-43b7-b6b3-a7826aa5e265'], 'covariate_ids': []}, {'id': 'f3b271ceb34641ec5cf88318800a17bf3362564ce454940baa913c56c034c4b15b9bdbcc32018add04918d4d878dececd0f0216c2d2e7a70b5a58088546b63f0', 'human_readable_id': 1, 'text': '.\n    When the failure rate crosses a configured threshold, the circuit\n    breaker temporarily blocks calls and allows recovery.', 'n_tokens': 23, 'document_id': 'b9c6f611addc84d60357c829e042254e47efbb01ea0825b99b0042d291db2339ea14650a903d05fc44a9f7e5bfc01460885d02298dbb5e34ecb6abbafe35d745', 'entity_ids': ['c1422f9b-4dee-45de-914b-af982169e32f'], 'relationship_ids': [], 'covariate_ids': []}, {'id': 'e0290ec1bd64a0f274583511d99c96326f49438a7d0593bb5adecc8f532d12f02fda092104f54e718fa9a12f90182f9826c40d2a1af0d8f5feecdb6e89f311d8', 'human_readable_id': 2, 'text': 'Distributed Systems: Observability\n\n    Observability helps engineering teams understand system behavior.\n    Metrics, logs, and distributed traces provide complementary evidence.\n\n    Latency measures request duration, while error rate measures the\n    proportion of failed requests. Service-level objectives define\n    target reliability for a service over a measurement window.\n\n    A service dashboard can combine latency, error rate, and traffic.\n    Distributed tracing follows a request across services and helps\n    identify which dependency contributes to elevated latency.', 'n_tokens': 97, 'document_id': 'e0290ec1bd64a0f274583511d99c96326f49438a7d0593bb5adecc8f532d12f02fda092104f54e718fa9a12f90182f9826c40d2a1af0d8f5feecdb6e89f311d8', 'entity_ids': ['2bfa1b99-09da-42de-b8f6-406c7da4e832'], 'relationship_ids': [], 'covariate_ids': []}, {'id': 'ef75e67bdfe9901dc928e64a03606b1720a71a57c77a80cd9d7b2b6c36f703e7ce4663519ca697ab2b1a56aa9382cc7475738ca88ef06860df7b6c402d82a89c', 'human_readable_id': 3, 'text': 'Distributed Systems: Resilience and Scaling\n\n    A service can become overloaded when incoming traffic exceeds capacity.\n    Rate limiting controls request volume, while load balancing distributes\n    traffic across healthy service instances.\n\n    Retries, exponential backoff, and circuit breakers are resilience\n    patterns. They should be configured together because retries can\n    increase traffic to an already overloaded dependency.\n\n    Monitoring latency, error rate, and traffic helps engineers detect\n    degradation. Scaling capacity may help with sustained load, but it', 'n_tokens': 100, 'document_id': '0a2ba140a34c27e2df00d56671272e108252f32cd0a4365c479bf4b339ce6182dc2e74434edef048c7db04213cb51998ab270f26780aed8166c388fc2acbfb34', 'entity_ids': ['b4b8a309-85d2-44f6-9b66-5db3a9aa5e75', '2bfa1b99-09da-42de-b8f6-406c7da4e832'], 'relationship_ids': ['bcba8bea-056a-48b5-a4ef-565de620ae0a'], 'covariate_ids': []}, {'id': 'f5c16f640b889b7a105cfec4770078f83371d21b92177253746e363a029c6e28d9d9924f4af997cea3d002c471a9bad04936774e63dfcb3715bf3f67696c0e90', 'human_readable_id': 4, 'text': ' Scaling capacity may help with sustained load, but it\n    does not fix every source of latency or dependency failure.', 'n_tokens': 23, 'document_id': '0a2ba140a34c27e2df00d56671272e108252f32cd0a4365c479bf4b339ce6182dc2e74434edef048c7db04213cb51998ab270f26780aed8166c388fc2acbfb34', 'entity_ids': [], 'relationship_ids': [], 'covariate_ids': []}]
